{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cec9aQfRo9zDfDP7GFZak","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-543 is closed. Summary of what this session did:\n\n## What I found\nThe build was already complete and committed on the branch (`8978b265` and earlier); a prior session had staged the close-ritual edits but was **reaped before committing** them. My job was to verify and finish the close honestly.\n\n## What I did\n1. **Verified the harness.** Commit bar green (smoke: 1442 passed / 8 skipped / 23.6 s, budget within 60 s). Ran the full unfiltered suite: **3199 passed, 24 skipped, 1 failed** in 586 s.\n\n2. **Investigated the one failure** — `test_derive_stage.py::test_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current`. Root cause: my WI's `8978b265` added TC-204 to `docs/test/test-cases.toml`, a **declared stage-derivation input**, staling the committed `docs/stage` fingerprint. This is an **expected work-branch condition, not a regression**:\n   - `docs/stage` is a trunk-lane-regenerated generated artifact; the `derived-stage` pre-commit step *skips on work branches* (\"generated freshness is the trunk lane's, §5.2\").\n   - `git log -- docs/stage` confirms it only moves on claim/mint/refresh trunk commits, never on a worker WI commit.\n   - The branch rules forbid a worker from regenerating it; the trunk lane re-derives it at merge and the test goes green on trunk.\n   - I **corrected the log fragment's inaccurate \"full suite green\" claim** to the honest result, and surfaced the latent gap (the dogfood test isn't work-branch-aware like the check step it mirrors) as a candidate OI — *not* fixed here, out of SR-163 scope.\n\n3. **Completed the close ritual:** Deliverable filled (before Context), `specref` cleared, approval brief confirmed idempotent (TC-204 as ADDED/Drafted), spec moved `active/ → archive/work/complete/` via the link-aware ritual, final commit `47579c89` carrying the `WI: WI-543` trailer. All pre